      'This Loan Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into between you, the borrower ("You" or "User"), and MAXIMERGE FINANCE LIMITED, a non-bank financial institution duly regulated under the laws of the Republic of Ghana, acting through its mobile application GhanaApp (the "Service Provider").\nBy selecting the checkbox “I accept the terms and conditions”, you acknowledge that you have carefully read, fully understood, and expressly agree to be legally bound by these Terms and Conditions ("T&Cs"), including any amendments or periodic updates that may be made. Your acceptance also constitutes authorization for MAXIMERGE FINANCE LIMITED to provide the loan in accordance with the terms set forth herein.\nPlease note:\na. These Terms and Conditions form a legally binding agreement between you, the Service Provider, and the lender, and shall be enforceable in accordance with the applicable laws of Ghana, having the same legal force and effect as a written, signed contract.\nb. MAXIMERGE FINANCE LIMITED acts as an authorized agent under this Agreement to collect processing fees and related charges on behalf of the Service Provider.\nYou further agree to execute or sign any additional documents, including but not limited to letters, undertakings, or supplementary agreements, as may be reasonably required by the lender to give full effect to or enforce the provisions of this Agreement。';
  static const String loanContractTermsTitle = 'A. Terms and Conditions';
  static const String loanContractTerms =
      '1.Loan Usage: You agree to utilize the loan amount granted by the lender under this Agreement strictly for the purpose and within the period stated in the approval letter.\n2. Loan Disbursement: The loan amount will be disbursed to the bank account or e-wallet account designated by you, as specified in your application.\n3. Credit Information Authorization: You hereby authorize the lender to obtain, verify, and update your credit information from the Ghana Credit Information Bureau or any other duly authorized institution, as necessary.\n4. Interest Payment: You are responsible for paying interest on the loan amount at the rate indicated in the approval letter. Interest shall accrue daily during the loan term and must be settled on the Due Date.\n5. Repayment of Principal and Interest: Both principal and accrued interest shall be repaid in full to the account specified in the approval letter on the Due Date.\n6. Late Payment: Failure to repay the loan principal and interest on the Due Date will result in a Late Fee being applied to the outstanding balance, as specified in the approval letter, until full payment is made.\n7. Change in Payment Method: The lender reserves the right to amend the payment method for any outstanding balance. You agree to comply with any revised payment instructions issued by the lender.\n8. Legal Action for Default: In the event of non-payment, the lender reserves the right to pursue all available legal remedies, including but not limited to litigation, equitable relief, or any other enforcement action permitted by law.\n9. Disclosure of Default: Upon default, the lender may, at its sole discretion, disclose your name and relevant details through appropriate channels as deemed necessary.\n10. Early Repayment: You may repay the loan in full prior to the Due Date, provided that both the outstanding principal and all accrued interest up to the prepayment date are fully settled.\n11. Responsibility for Outstanding Balances: You acknowledge and agree that you remain fully responsible for repaying all outstanding amounts at any time, irrespective of prior payments, claims, or notifications from the lender or Service Provider.\n12. No Right to Withhold Payment: You agree that, under no circumstances, shall you refuse or delay repayment to the lender in accordance with these terms and conditions.\n13. False or Misleading Information: If any information provided by you in connection with the loan is found to be false, inaccurate, or misleading, the lender may, at its discretion, demand immediate repayment of the loan and all related outstanding amounts.\n14. Communications: You consent to receiving notifications, updates, and other communications from the lender or Service Provider via your registered mobile number or email address.\n15. Taxes and Other Payments: If the lender pays any taxes or other charges on your behalf to a governmental or regulatory authority in relation to the loan, you agree to promptly reimburse the lender for such payments.\n16. Assignment of Rights: The lender reserves the absolute right to assign, sell, or transfer its rights and obligations under this Agreement to any third party. You agree to honor all obligations owed to such assignee.\n17. Non-Transferability: You may not assign, sell, or transfer your rights or obligations under this Agreement to any other person without the lender’s prior written consent.\n18. Amendment of Terms: The lender may amend these terms and conditions from time to time. Any such changes will be communicated to you and shall take effect only after you have been duly notified.\n19. Effective Date: These terms and conditions take effect from the date of execution and shall remain valid until all obligations hereunder are fully discharged.\n20. Governing Law: This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Ghana.';
